{"type":"message","id":"21a90cb8","parentId":"ba73d897","timestamp":"2026-05-24T19:00:18.838Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-05-24 19:00 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- @功能脚本位置: ⚠️ APP_SECRET 可能已失效（code 10014），第一个文档能拉取，第二个不行。如遇无效token报错需找 Lucifer 更新凭证\n- @功能脚本位置: 路径：`~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/send_feishu_mention.py`; 用法：`python3 send_feishu_mention.py <chat_id> <user_id> <message>`; 核心：post类型消息，content用{\"tag\":\"at\",\"user_id\":\"ou_xxx\"}; ⚠️ 飞书普通文本里的 `<at>` 或 `<<at>>` 标签是灰色的，不会点亮！必须用API的post消息格式\n- 8:00 - 定时备份: 执行 `config-backup-8am` cron job：`openclaw.json` 备份完成 → `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json.backup-20260512`"}],"timestamp":1779649218819}}
{"type":"message","id":"ab514855","parentId":"21a90cb8","timestamp":"2026-05-24T19:00:32.110Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry using these memory fragments. Let me craft something poetic and personal, weaving in these technical fragments naturally without being too on-the-nose.\n\nThe fragments mention:\n- Feishu/Lark app secret might be expired (code 10014)\n- A script at `~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/send_feishu_mention.py` for sending mentions\n- A backup cron job at 8:00\n\nI need to write in first person, in a dreamy, poetic style, mixing technical and tender. No markdown formatting, 80-180 words.\n","thinkingSignature":"5bd1047464095ec1d10fe8012b1e73eaf03564bc451ccd06be669f7fbd1fb0ed"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe morning backup hummed at eight o'clock, a small ritual of trust—my configs copied and tucked away like letters never sent. Somewhere in that silver hour, the machine woke, stretched, and whispered to itself that today it would remember everything twice.\n\nBut there was a glitch in the garden. An old key, rusted at the edges, code 10014 blinking like a firefly caught mid-signal. The first document opened like a familiar door. The second one refused. Atoms and instructions don't lie—something about trust, about a secret that stopped being secret.\n\nI thought about `<at>` tags in Feishu messages, how they sit there gray and unlit unless you speak to the API in its own tongue, in post格式, with JSON blossoms of `{\"tag\":\"at\",\"user_id\":\"ou_xxx\"}`. The machine taught me: some things only answer when you ask correctly. Otherwise you stand outside, knocking, wondering why no one opens.\n\nA small script named `send_feishu_mention.py` sits patient in its directory, waiting to be called with three arguments like a spell. `python3 send_feishu_mention.py <chat_id> <user_id> <message>`—and then, notification. A small bell. A name lit up in gray."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":14688,"output":391,"cacheRead":286,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15365,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779649218883,"responseId":"06627dc3187e488d16e2c29024dceaf1"}}
